---
import type { CollectionEntry } from 'astro:content';

type Props = { brand: CollectionEntry<'brand'>['data'] };
const { brand } = Astro.props;

const proofRails = ['Context before charisma', 'Permissioned evidence only', 'Named system, not service list', 'One useful next decision'];
const railRows = [
  { old: 'More visibility', next: 'Better interpretation', copy: 'Make the work easy for the right person to explain, forward, and remember.' },
  { old: 'More credentials', next: 'One clear receipt', copy: 'Replace accumulation with the single case, result, or decision that proves the difference.' },
  { old: 'More services', next: 'One useful system', copy: 'Turn expertise into a sequence a buyer can evaluate before they ever meet you.' },
];
const stack = [
  { n: '01', title: 'Tension', text: 'Name the problem the room already feels but has not yet made legible.' },
  { n: '02', title: 'Break', text: 'Show which familiar assumption is now producing the wrong outcome.' },
  { n: '03', title: 'Model', text: 'Give the better sequence a name, a shape, and a decision logic.' },
  { n: '04', title: 'Receipt', text: 'Present the permissioned result that makes the model safe to take seriously.' },
];
const dossiers = [
  { n: '01', title: 'The initial condition', text: 'What was true before the work began—and why did it matter?' },
  { n: '02', title: 'The intervention', text: 'Which decision, asset, framework, or room changed?' },
  { n: '03', title: 'The observed shift', text: 'What can the client actually approve for public use?' },
];
---

<section class="pmh-hero">
  <div class="pmh-utility"><span>RAGHAVAN ADVISORY / PROOF MACHINE</span><span>CONCEPTUAL PRODUCTION DEMO</span><span>THE SIGNAL STACK / 01</span></div>
  <div class="pmh-hero__copy">
    <p class="pmh-kicker">Executive authority, made legible</p>
    <h1>THE WORK IS<br />REAL.<br /><em>THE SIGNAL</em><br />IS NOT.</h1>
    <p class="pmh-deck">For leaders whose best decisions are visible only to the people already in the room. We turn the record into a position, a proof library, and a system the market can understand without an introduction.</p>
    <div class="pmh-actions"><a href="#signal-stack">See the Signal Stack <span>↓</span></a><a href="/case-studies/" class="pmh-actions__secondary">Open case files ↗</a></div>
    <p class="pmh-safety">Concept demo. Production claims require permissioned evidence.</p>
  </div>
  <figure class="pmh-hero__image"><img src="/images/portrait-hero-insitu.webp" alt="Conceptual strategist in an executive working environment" width="1600" height="1000" /><figcaption>REAL WORK / CLEAR SIGNAL<br />NO BORROWED AUTHORITY</figcaption></figure>
  <div class="pmh-hero__edge">THE MARKET<br />CANNOT VALUE<br />WHAT IT<br />CANNOT READ.</div>
</section>

<section class="pmh-rail" aria-label="Proof Machine operating principles">{proofRails.map((item, index) => <span><b>{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</b>{item}</span>)}</section>

<section class="pmh-intro">
  <div><p class="pmh-kicker">The actual problem</p><h2>YOU DO NOT<br />NEED TO BE<br /><em>LOUDER.</em></h2></div>
  <p>Most personal-brand advice mistakes exposure for authority. The problem is usually not a lack of activity. It is a lack of usable evidence: no clear position, no language for the value created, no named mechanism, and no record a stranger can trust.</p>
  <span class="pmh-intro__note">THE PROOF MACHINE STARTS WITH THE RECORD, NOT THE FEED.</span>
</section>

<section class="pmh-replace">
  <header><p class="pmh-kicker">Replace the model</p><h2>STOP<br />ADDING.<br /><em>START<br />SIGNALING.</em></h2></header>
  <div class="pmh-replace__rows">
    {railRows.map((row, index) => <article><div><span>OLD MODEL / {String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span><h3>{row.old}</h3></div><b>×</b><div><span>BETTER MODEL / {String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span><h3>{row.next}</h3><p>{row.copy}</p></div></article>)}
  </div>
</section>

<section id="signal-stack" class="pmh-stack">
  <div class="pmh-stack__head"><p class="pmh-kicker">The named system</p><h2>THE<br />SIGNAL<br /><em>STACK.</em></h2><p>Four layers turn an expert’s private judgement into a public asset. The sequence is the product: skip a layer and the market gets an incomplete story.</p><a href="/method/">Read the system in full ↗</a></div>
  <div class="pmh-stack__grid">{stack.map((item) => <article><span>{item.n}</span><h3>{item.title}</h3><p>{item.text}</p></article>)}<div class="pmh-stack__core">THE<br />RECORD</div></div>
</section>

<section class="pmh-files">
  <div class="pmh-files__heading"><p class="pmh-kicker">How proof actually works</p><h2>A CASE FILE<br />IS NOT A<br /><em>TESTIMONIAL.</em></h2><p>It is a compact, permissioned argument. Every public case needs a clear initial condition, an intervention someone can understand, and an observed result the client allows you to share.</p><a href="/case-studies/">See the case-study system ↗</a></div>
  <figure class="pmh-files__photo"><img src="/images/workshop.webp" alt="Conceptual strategic workshop showing the work in action" width="1920" height="1280" /><figcaption>THE WORKING VIEW / A RECORD IN CONTEXT</figcaption></figure>
  <div class="pmh-files__dossiers">{dossiers.map((item) => <article><b>{item.n}</b><h3>{item.title}</h3><p>{item.text}</p></article>)}</div>
</section>

<section class="pmh-ledger">
  <div class="pmh-ledger__title"><p class="pmh-kicker">The evidence ledger</p><h2>WHAT IS<br />SAFE TO<br /><em>BELIEVE?</em></h2></div>
  <div class="pmh-ledger__table"><div class="pmh-ledger__head"><span>Evidence type</span><span>What it proves</span><span>Production rule</span></div><div><strong>Decision record</strong><p>A meaningful choice and its stakes</p><small>Show enough context to make the decision real.</small></div><div><strong>Outcome data</strong><p>A change the client can substantiate</p><small>Use source, window, and permission—not inflated shorthand.</small></div><div><strong>Third-party signal</strong><p>How credible others interpret the work</p><small>Attribute precisely; do not create a borrowed-authority wall.</small></div><div><strong>Named method</strong><p>How the work becomes repeatable</p><small>State the mechanism, inputs, and output—not a vague promise.</small></div></div>
</section>

<section class="pmh-working">
  <div class="pmh-working__image"><img src="/images/portrait-story.webp" alt="Conceptual advisor in a working environment" width="1920" height="1440" /></div>
  <div class="pmh-working__copy"><p class="pmh-kicker">The person behind the system</p><h2>THE WORK<br />IS NOT TO<br />MAKE YOU<br /><em>LOOK</em><br />IMPORTANT.</h2><p>It is to identify the value already present in the record, make a defensible claim around it, and give the right rooms a way to act on it. The result should feel less like a campaign and more like an operating system.</p><a href="/about/">Read the record ↗</a></div>
</section>

<section class="pmh-diagnostic">
  <p class="pmh-kicker">The next practical move</p><h2>WHAT IS<br />THE MARKET<br /><em>MISSING?</em></h2><p>Use the diagnostic to identify whether the immediate gap is position, proof, package, or platform. In production, this becomes a live form or direct booking path.</p><a href="/contact/">Run the diagnostic ↗</a><span>Conceptual site demo / no visitor data is collected until a real endpoint is configured.</span>
</section>

<style>
  .pmh-hero { position:relative; display:grid; grid-template-columns:1.06fr .94fr; min-height:calc(100svh - 4.2rem); overflow:hidden; background:#f1f1eb; color:#101114; border-bottom:1px solid #101114; } .pmh-utility { position:absolute; z-index:4; top:0; left:0; right:0; display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr 1fr; gap:1rem; padding:.8rem clamp(1rem,3vw,3.2rem); border-bottom:1px solid #101114; font-family:var(--font-display); font-size:.56rem; font-weight:800; letter-spacing:.13em; text-transform:uppercase; } .pmh-utility span:nth-child(2) { color:#0b32a8; text-align:center; } .pmh-utility span:last-child { color:#55575a; text-align:right; }
  .pmh-hero__copy { position:relative; z-index:2; display:grid; align-content:end; padding:clamp(8rem,14vh,10rem) clamp(1.25rem,5vw,6rem) clamp(3.5rem,8vw,7rem); } .pmh-kicker { margin:0; color:#0b32a8; font-family:var(--font-display); font-size:.62rem; font-weight:800; letter-spacing:.14em; text-transform:uppercase; } .pmh-hero h1,.pmh-intro h2,.pmh-replace h2,.pmh-stack h2,.pmh-files h2,.pmh-ledger h2,.pmh-working h2,.pmh-diagnostic h2 { margin:1.2rem 0 0; font-family:var(--font-display); font-size:clamp(3.9rem,8.9vw,10.6rem); font-weight:800; line-height:.73; letter-spacing:-.1em; text-transform:uppercase; } .pmh-hero h1 em,.pmh-intro h2 em,.pmh-replace h2 em,.pmh-stack h2 em,.pmh-files h2 em,.pmh-ledger h2 em,.pmh-working h2 em,.pmh-diagnostic h2 em { color:#0b32a8; font-family:var(--font-serif); font-weight:400; letter-spacing:-.12em; } .pmh-deck { max-width:32rem; margin:2rem 0 0; color:#505256; font-size:1.04rem; line-height:1.68; } .pmh-actions { display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:1rem; margin-top:2rem; } .pmh-actions a,.pmh-stack__head a,.pmh-files__heading a,.pmh-working__copy a,.pmh-diagnostic a { display:inline-block; padding:.9rem 1rem; background:#0b32a8; color:#fff; font-family:var(--font-display); font-size:.62rem; font-weight:800; letter-spacing:.13em; text-transform:uppercase; } .pmh-actions a:hover,.pmh-stack__head a:hover,.pmh-files__heading a:hover,.pmh-working__copy a:hover,.pmh-diagnostic a:hover { background:#101114; } .pmh-actions .pmh-actions__secondary { background:transparent; color:#101114; border:1px solid #101114; } .pmh-safety { margin:1.5rem 0 0; color:#737572; font-family:var(--font-display); font-size:.52rem; font-weight:800; letter-spacing:.1em; text-transform:uppercase; }
